<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms buy 21,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms buy 21,500 tonnes of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd jointly bought on Friday 21,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Mitsubishi Corp, company officials said.  </p>
<p> DRV    Of the total, Cheiljedang bought 8,500 tonnes at basis</p>
<p>prices over September futures on the U.S. grain futures exchanges including the Chicago Board of Trade, they said.</p>
<p>Dongah bought the remaining 13,000 tonnes at fixed prices, they said.</p>
<p>Shipment was set for July 20-August 20 to the southeastern port of Pusan.</p>
<p>Results of the tenders are as follows:  </p>
<p>Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Tonne(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		5,500   $149.90</p>
<p>(ordinary)</p>
<p>  Soft White		1,800   $149.90</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5 pct)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,300   $162.20</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  2,400   $184.75 Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Bushel(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		2,500   $0.4520 (over CBOT's Sept)</p>
<p>(ordinary)</p>
<p>  Soft White		1,000   $0.4520 (over CBOT's Sept)</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5 pct)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 2,500   $0.6195 (over KCBT's Sept) Dark</p>
<p>Northern Spring  2,500   $1.0955 (over MGE's Sept)   --Seoul</p>
